# Prove by SAT that the *sky130hd-mapped* netlist of `requantize` computes the
# same function as the RTL, for every input.
#
# synth/equiv_conv5x5_pe.ys and friends compare the RTL against the generic
# netlist -- `techmap` output, no real cell library, structure largely intact.
# This script compares it against the netlist that docs/PPA.md reports area and
# timing for: `dfflibmap` + `abc -liberty` mapping onto real sky130hd standard
# cells, at the same 10 ns target run_ppa.sh uses. That mapping is where a
# synthesis bug would actually live, and it is a far more aggressive
# transformation -- abc restructures the logic entirely, so the netlist below
# is built from maj3/xnor3/a211oi cells that have no counterpart in the RTL.
#
# The price of that is the equivalence-point count. equiv_make pairs signals by
# name; generic mapping leaves internal names intact (694 points on conv5x5_pe),
# while abc leaves nothing but the ports. So this proof has 8 points, one per
# output bit, and each is a full input-cone SAT problem over all 39 input bits
# rather than a cheap match against a neighbouring node. Fewer points here means
# a harder proof, not a weaker one.
#
# That is also why only two blocks have a script like this. Unbounded
# equivalence over a mapped multiply-accumulate is a classic hard SAT instance:
# conv5x5_row_mac did not converge in 20 minutes, and neither did the two blocks
# containing it. Those netlists are covered by simulation instead -- see
# `make gls` and docs/VERIFICATION_PLAN.md. Arithmetic-aware datapath matching
# is precisely what commercial LEC has and `equiv_simple` does not.
#
# ORFS_ROOT is hard-coded here because yosys scripts take no parameters; change
# the three liberty paths together if the PDK lives elsewhere.

# ---- gold: the RTL -----------------------------------------------------------
read_verilog -sv rtl/requantize.sv
hierarchy -check -top requantize
proc
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gold

# ---- gate: the sky130hd-mapped netlist ---------------------------------------
# read_liberty -lib loads the cell interfaces as blackboxes, which is what abc
# and dfflibmap need. Reading the same liberty again with -overwrite replaces
# those blackboxes with each cell's `function` as real logic; without that step
# the cells have no SAT model and equiv_simple has nothing to reason about.
design -reset
read_liberty -lib /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
read_verilog -sv rtl/requantize.sv
hierarchy -check -top requantize
synth -top requantize -flatten
dfflibmap -liberty /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
abc -liberty /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib -D 10000
setundef -zero
opt_clean -purge
stat -liberty /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
read_liberty -overwrite -ignore_miss_func -ignore_miss_dir -ignore_miss_data_latch -ignore_buses /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
hierarchy -check -top requantize
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gate

# ---- compare -----------------------------------------------------------------
design -copy-from gold -as gold requantize
design -copy-from gate -as gate requantize
equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
# equiv_struct merges structurally identical nodes first, which recovers a few
# match points abc's renaming lost and keeps the SAT cones smaller.
equiv_struct
equiv_simple -short
equiv_struct
equiv_simple
equiv_induct
# -assert is the whole check. Without it equiv_status prints the unproven count
# and exits 0, so the target would pass on a netlist that was never proven.
equiv_status -assert
